# Play view with 11 timelines (tests/ui/records/play-view-11tl.5dr: Standard, T5w, ten present boards of which nine must move, L-6 inactive): squares stay
# at 20 px (the multiverse view's Overview draws them 4.5 px), the inactive timeline is a chip in the collapsed row at the bottom and a click on it
# shows its board in the inspector. "Start turns in Play view" is switched on first, so the game opens in the Play view.
startplayview on
record ../records/play-view-11tl.5dr
wait 90
zoom?
capture play-view-11tl-start
key SPACE
wait 10
key SPACE
wait 10
capture play-view-11tl-cursor         # Space moves the keyboard cursor over the boards that need a move
key DOWN
wait 10
key RIGHT
wait 10
capture play-view-11tl-arrows
pvclick chip -6 6
wait 20
capture play-view-11tl-inactive       # the inactive timeline's board in the inspector
clicksq -5 8 g4
wait 20
capture play-view-11tl-select         # a lifted piece whose target is on the inactive board: the dock shows it with its dots
